// Fairy Forest's park (verse/fairy-forest/README.md): its layout in metres,
// the paths, the stream's course, the glades, the faded flower patches, the
// creatures and their troubles, and the fade: colour comes back in circles
// that spread out from what you bloom. The page (apps/openagents-web/fairy.coax)
// loads this file, draws it and runs it; fairy.wgsl reads the circles (Bloom)
// to drain or restore colour.
//
// The land is Central Park at a quarter of its size: 1025 m from 59th
// Street (south, -z) to 110th (north, +z) and 208 m from Central Park West
// (-x) to Fifth Avenue (+x), with its lakes, drives, footpaths and
// landmarks where they are in the real park (verse/fairy-forest/park.coax).
// The heart tree is the origin, in the Ramble. Five glades: Mossbank (where
// you wake, by the Pond), The Reeds (at the Pool), Lanternwood (the North
// Woods), Thornfall (brambles and a fallen giant tree, at the north edge)
// and the Old Ring (standing stones, by Cleopatra's Needle). The fade is
// only round them and the heart tree (FF_FADE); the rest of the park keeps
// its colour. Each glade's creature has one trouble: its glade has faded.
// Bloom its patches and it is happy again, and one of the heart tree's five
// roots wakes. All five, and the heart tree blooms: the ending. The park
// stays open after it.
//   coax/bin/coax test apps/openagents-web/fairy.coax   (this file's checks run with the page's)

// The ground: a rectangle 80 cells of 3 m west to east and 354 south to
// north, the park (verse/fairy-forest/park.coax) and the streets round it.
FF_CELLS :: 80;
FF_ROWS :: 354;
FF_CELL :: 3.0;
FF_WEST :: -120.0;
FF_SOUTH :: -380.0;
FF_EDGE :: FF_WEST;
// The park's walls, where you may walk to: Central Park West, Fifth Avenue,
// Central Park South (59th Street) and Central Park North (110th Street).
FF_PARK_W :: -104.0; FF_PARK_E :: 104.0; FF_PARK_S :: -362.0; FF_PARK_N :: 663.0;
FF_PATH_HALF :: 1.4;       // a footpath's half width
FF_GROUND_POINTS :: (FF_CELLS + 1) * (FF_ROWS + 1);
FF_LEVEL :: -0.3;          // the water's surface: the stream, the pond and the lakes
FF_LAYOUT :: 2;            // the layout a kept place belongs to (the park); a place kept in the old valley goes back to the spawn

// The paths: the heart tree's ring, the park's drives (kind 1), the Mall
